// xpute's link in WIT's shape; the execution meaning is xpute's (xpute-link
// link.rs). WIT's grammar is used as far as xpute needs it: interfaces, `func`
// and `async func`, resources and their methods, records, enums, variants,
// lists, options, results, bool, the integers of every width, f32, f64 and
// strings.
//
// Whatever is called is an object, under a handle. A singleton interface's is
// named: `frame.json5`'s `NAMED` bit and the hash of its package and its name,
// ("xpute:clocks", "monotonic-clock"), which the generator writes on both
// sides, so it is called with no open. A resource's the side that implements
// it issues, opened by a URI: a tuple of tokens, each an s32 or a string, as a
// file's are the program's path tokens; or answered by a function that returns
// it. A frame's command carries the handle, the method's number and the `RES`
// bit (31): the handle in bits 8..30, the method in bits 0..7. A method's
// number is its place in its interface, in declaration order: a singleton
// interface's functions, or one resource's methods.
//
// The root, handle 0, has three methods. `open(uri) -> handle`, number 0, the
// implementing side answers at once from the opener mounted at the URI's
// longest matching leading tokens. An open is pipelined, so a missing file
// opens, and its first method with a result answers `no-entry`. `cancel(tag)`,
// number 1, cancels a call the sender has pending (`frame.json5` `CANCEL`).
// `open-at(handle, k, uri)`, number 2, opens an object under a handle the
// sender issued, by the receiver's `k`th opener: what a runtime that stands in
// for a UI on another thread sends that UI's end once it has answered the
// guest's open (`frame.json5` `OPEN_AT`).
// Every handle has a drop, method 0xFF, as the component model's resource
// drop, which takes no result and lets the object go; a resource whose end
// must report a result keeps its own method for it, as a file's `close`.
//
// A guest has three exports. `link_init` lays the link and answers its layout,
// the inbox and a frame's cap, and runs nothing of the program. `link_boot` is
// the guest's first entry: the program's boot mounts its implementations, and
// only then does the entry start. An interface is called by its named handle
// with no open (`frame.json5` `NAMED`), so a bug in a boot is reported through
// the stop at once. `link_in` enters the guest with the frame laid in its
// inbox. The host calls init, reads the layout, then boot, so every entry
// comes from a host that knows the cap. A trap out of any export stops the
// guest for good.
//
// A method that may answer later is an `async func`, and is sent; any other
// always answers at once. An `async func` always answers later, with
// EINPROGRESS, so waiting on one leaves the guest's entry. The guest runs only
// when the host enters it: with a request, an answer, or the answer of what it
// armed, such as `monotonic-clock.wait-for`.
//
// Raw memory enters WIT in one place, `xpute:link/types.lent`: a borrow, in the
// component model's sense, of a buffer in the caller's memory, (buf, nbyte), valid
// until the answer; an empty buffer has no address, and is (0, 0). Its address
// is a u64 on every platform, one layout everywhere: a module's offset into
// its own memory, a native guest's pointer. The data stays
// where it is and only its place crosses; the callee reads or writes it there.
// The caller's binding takes a buffer it owns, lends it with the call and hands
// it back with the answer, so the borrow lasts as long as the ownership. A call
// dropped before its answer is canceled (`frame.json5` `CANCEL`), as the
// component model cancels a dropped subtask, and keeps the buffer alive until
// its answer, ECANCELED or its own, comes.
//
// A packet lays its values out as the Component Model's Canonical ABI does
// (xpute-link cabi.rs): a call's args as one tuple, an answer's value alone,
// each value at its type's alignment, an enum, an option or a result as a
// variant, its discriminant first. A string's or a list's bytes lie past the
// packet's fixed part, its pointer an offset from the packet's start, where
// the ABI copies them into the callee's memory; a lent buffer stays where it
// is. The answer's result is a status: 0, EINPROGRESS, the errno the call
// was refused with, by the link or by the method as a caller's bug (EINVAL,
// where the ABI traps), or a method's errno where its WIT has no `result`; a
// method with a `result` answers any other failure as its error case.
// TypeScript's null is an option's none, so no option holds an option.
//
// The link's crossings (xpute-guest link.rs) are no world's: a world holds
// only interfaces, and a program's world only those it uses.

package xpute:link@0.1.0;

// What the link itself takes.
interface types {
  // A URI's token.
  variant token {
    int(s32),
    str(string),
  }

  // A borrow of a buffer in the caller's memory, valid until the answer.
  record lent {
    buf: u64,
    nbyte: u32,
  }
}
